{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination","id":1097768,"title":"Lunar Cloning - no items, fox only, final destination","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T07:35:10-07:00","id":1097768,"title":"Lunar Cloning - no items, fox only, final destination","content":"Even if the Lunar Exalted have an easier time multiplying themselves into a battle group than Solars do of approximating the Flash's &quot;I'm everywhere at once&quot; trick (Faster Than Self Technique), they naturally suffer their own limitations. Such as a possible inability to create copies of their weapons.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted have never had an effect quite like Glorious Solar Saber, because a Dexterity Charm tree doesn't impose the same limitations as a Melee Charm tree. It is not appropriate for the Lunar Exalted to have a Green Lantern power which allows them to conjure any object or tool they might need, the way that Infernal Exalted could with the Charms of She Who Lives In Her Name. This is also a big part of the reason the Lunar Exalted cannot have anything approximating Phantom-Conjuring Performance.<br /> <br /> A Solar using Faster Than Self Technique could run into an ammunition problem if using a single bow and quiver, but at least he could use a single bow. A Lunar with a single bow may be left with just one bow and a lot of empty hands.<br /> <br /> Both the Solar and Lunar have the option of scavenging the battlefield for enough munitions, but more often than not, the Lunar might simply resort to becoming a battle group of beasts, armed with tooth and claw.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can a Lunar clone fake a Lunar's clothing? The clones should dissolve into motes of Essence after they die or expire, so the Lunar can't run a textile business by copying a few really expensive dresses.<br /> <br /> <br /> But there's more. Since Lunar cloning could be so much easier for them than Faster Than Self Technique is for Solars, lesser forms of it can appear much earlier in the Lunar Charmset to help give them a very different experience than the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> For one thing, it wouldn't be found in their &quot;Athletics&quot; Charms, but at an intersection of their Evasion and Extra Attack Charms.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted need to use False Image Feint and Ebon Shadow Style's Shadow-Body Dissolution to perform the phantom Clone / Replacement technique, where the enemy strikes only an afterimage or illusion as the Solar watches from concealment. But the Lunar Exalted could produce an actual doppleganger to take the blow for them while they use the opportunity to re-establish surprise, like <i>RWBY's</i> Blake Belladonna and her Shadow Semblance.<br /> <br /> Though if the Lunar cannot copy his clothes or weapons, he might not be able to pull off Blake's trick except when he starts in an animal form. Not unless he leaves his clothes and weapons with the clone while he himself tries to enter concealment as an animal small enough to evade being seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clones also spice up Lunar attacks! Invincible Fury of the Dawn allows a Solar to move one range band per attack in the Extra Attack flurry, leaping around with spear or dagger. But a Lunar might instead burst into a temporary group of clones that simultaneously leap in completely different directions to attack their own targets.<br /> <br /> Which of course leads to questions of what happens when a target successfully clashes a clone. It would be a major advantage for the Lunar to be effectively immune to the dangers of clashing opponents by sending clones to do it for him. But then, if killing a clone hurt a Lunar, there would be no point in using them for dodging distractions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> FINAL DESTINATION<br /> <br /> Alchemical Exalted would approach the matter between the Lunar and Solar methods. Their Charm structures would work more like Lunars, with the &quot;I'm an army of one&quot; Charm being found in &quot;Evasion and Extra Action&quot; rather than &quot;Athletics&quot;, but their &quot;quantum super-positioning&quot; trick would allow them to &quot;copy&quot; their weapons like Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:19:17-07:00","id":1097782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination#post1097768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, if killing a clone hurt a Lunar, there would be no point in using them for dodging distractions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not remotely true, especially given that we now have two entirely separate damage tracks - perhaps a Lunar whose clone is killed takes three points of Initiative damage from the shock; it's not great, sure, but it's a hell of a lot better than what the hatchet would have done if it hit the original!<br /> <br /> Personally I'm not too sold on examining Faster Than Self to construct one's model for an equivalent Lunar Charm, especially since having it be unable to clone equipment will just lead to more &quot;Silver Solar&quot; mentality. Might be better to just blaze a new trail entirely, even if it gets to the same place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-28-2017, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:36:01-07:00","id":1097784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097782#post1097782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not remotely true, especially given that we now have two entirely separate damage tracks - perhaps a Lunar whose clone is killed takes three points of Initiative damage from the shock; it's not great, sure, but it's a hell of a lot better than what the hatchet would have done if it hit the original!</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I'm not too sold on examining Faster Than Self specifically to construct one's model for a Lunar Charm </div> </div> </div>Vance didn't think that Lunar Charms would turn them into battle groups until that Charm came out, and afterwards he said he'd be surprised if they didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> especially since having it be unable to clone equipment will just lead to more &quot;Silver Solar&quot; mentality. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I forgot to mention the advantage that the Lunar version would have: Compatibility with Stamina Charms.<br /> <br /> Faster Than Self Technique has to forbid interaction with any Resistance Charms that aren't permanent or Simple; the permanent Ox-Bodies are excluded since the Solar is set at Magnitude 10 regardless of Health Levels, and any Simple-type Resistance Charms need to be activated beforehand. Further, the Solar suffers a penalty to Athletics actions for three turns after Faster Than Self ends.<br /> <br /> The Lunar doesn't necessarily have that problem, since he's not actually running around pretending to multiple people at once. He actually is in multiple places at once, simultaneously. Much less exhausting.<br /> <br /> The Lunar might also be able to use the Stamina health-regeneration Charms to recover Magnitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:45:25-07:00","id":1097787,"title":"","content":"Vance wasn't a developer before that Charm came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T12:35:43-07:00","id":1097844,"title":"","content":"So, why wouldn't <i>you </i>want to model mass Lunar cloning in a fashion similar to how Faster Than Self does it? What part do you disagree with?<br /> <br /> The large mote cost?<br /> <br /> The per-turn mote tax?<br /> <br /> Modeling the sheer number of bodies as a battle-group as opposed to a number of independent bodies? Giving a Lunar player the ability to act three or more times every round seems a tad much.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:09:48-07:00","id":1097851,"title":"","content":"You'll probably disagree, but I think I would represent Lunar cloning as a bit more fine-tuned than Faster than Self. The Lunar might not be able to make dozens or hundreds of duplicates (to fill out a large battlegroup) but would instead make a much smaller number, however in turn those clones would be much more powerful. They'd be able to use many of her powers and almost act as secondary characters in their own right rather than just random mass combat filler like Solars get.<br /> <br /> The end result would be the Lunar creating a duplicate of himself that's capable of using at least some of the Lunars powers and abilities, with some built in limitations of course. Perhaps the Lunar could even transfer her soul and Essence between clones. I might even make a short &quot;I create creatures&quot; tree, which allows the Lunar to create duplicates of creatures and people he's drank the hearts blood of. Duplicating himself, or at least in such a way that the duplicate gets access to his magical powers, would probably come a bit later in such a Charmtree.<br /> <br /> I also think that if I were to make a &quot;Lunar turns into a mass combat unit&quot; I would probably prefer to have the Lunar turn into swarm of animals or something, rather than starting by copying Faster Than Self Technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:05:20-07:00","id":1097881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097851#post1097851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably disagree, but I think I would represent Lunar cloning as a bit more fine-tuned than Faster than Self. The Lunar might not be able to make dozens or hundreds of duplicates (to fill out a large battlegroup) but would instead make a much smaller number, however in turn those clones would be much more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>A <i>small </i>battle-group <i>is </i>closer to what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> Since I'd like Lunars to have this power sooner than something like Faster Than Self, and also to be able to use Stamina Charms as a battle-group, I figured that starting at the bare minimum size of Size 1 was acceptable. The Lunar could potentially increase the Size through upgrades or special conditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They'd be able to use many of her powers and almost act as secondary characters in their own right rather than just random mass combat filler like Solars get. </div> </div> </div>I think the power to make a permanent familiar of such intelligence and power would be a greater trick than a single-minded battle-group of temporary clones.<br /> <br /> Better to look to those Solar Occult Charms about building spirits, for terms of balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think that if I were to make a &quot;Lunar turns into a mass combat unit&quot; I would probably prefer to have the Lunar turn into swarm of animals or something, rather than starting by copying Faster Than Self Technique. </div> </div> </div>Splitting apart into an equal mass of small animals is a different and compatible trick. Becoming a battle-group of bees would require <i>both </i>Becoming the Swarm as well as &quot;Ant and Starfish Trick&quot;.<br /> <br /> But for becoming a large group of creatures at least as large as a wolf, the best way to model such a thing is a battle-group. That's why battle-groups exist!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:05:51-07:00","id":1097896,"title":"","content":"Oh, I think Lunars should be able to do the whole &quot;I turn into a battlegroup.&quot; Just that I would lean in a direction other than, &quot;I bring forth an army of identical clones to form a battlegroup,&quot; like turning into battlegroup of animals, or swarms of insects or that kind of thing. There are a lot of interesting things to do with clones, but I think as far as turning into a battlegroup, Lunars have other, more interesting options than clones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:19:00-07:00","id":1097908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097896#post1097896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I think Lunars should be able to do the whole &quot;I turn into a battlegroup.&quot; Just that I would lean in a direction other than, &quot;I bring forth an army of identical clones to form a battlegroup,&quot; like turning into battlegroup of animals, or swarms of insects or that kind of thing. There are a lot of interesting things to do with clones, but I think as far as turning into a battlegroup, Lunars have other, more interesting options than clones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you understand that my idea of clone is appearance agnostic, and that I'm very much envisioning a Lunar becoming a battle group of animals?<br /> <br /> I even talked about how the Lunar Exalted might not be able to effectively use their natural human forms in this manner, since in that case their human-form clones would likely be naked and unarmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:09:44-07:00","id":1097934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097881#post1097881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <i>small </i>battle-group <i>is </i>closer to what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> Since I'd like Lunars to have this power sooner than something like Faster Than Self, and also to be able to use Stamina Charms as a battle-group, I figured that starting at the bare minimum size of Size 1 was acceptable. The Lunar could potentially increase the Size through upgrades or special conditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the power to make a permanent familiar of such intelligence and power would be a greater trick than a single-minded battle-group of temporary clones.<br /> <br /> Better to look to those Solar Occult Charms about building spirits, for terms of balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Splitting apart into an equal mass of small animals is a different and compatible trick. Becoming a battle-group of bees would require <i>both </i>Becoming the Swarm as well as &quot;Ant and Starfish Trick&quot;.<br /> <br /> But for becoming a large group of creatures at least as large as a wolf, the best way to model such a thing is a battle-group. That's why battle-groups exist!</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> Make it cheap but the clones on default are trash. You aren't making more you, you are making MINIONS. Or calling up dogs. Loayal amazing well trained dogs that can literally smell your orders or faithfully keep to a task like &quot;watch the master's back&quot; But still you can't make multiple lunars.<br /> <br /> I get my &quot;elephant into a large group of big cats&quot; might not be ideal. And man this seems tied into 3e. But I think you are cart before the horsing. Think of the effect and how you want to model it. Then think about how the splat type would be affected with the ability.<br /> THEN see &quot;does this outperform Solar equivalents&quot;<br /> <br /> Being able to summon a horde of rats or pack of wolves or pride of lions that listens and coordinates with you is no laughing matter (if animal stats didn't suck) But at the same time its relatively easy to counter.<br /> <br /> That said to follow your proposal? Assume the Naruto model. The clones can be large in number but they are as durable as gossamer. They retain armor and soal.. BUT if this is overwhlemed they go up in smoke as beneath there is not the necessary substance of motes. If kept alive or fed (stamina or weight) they can stay but then.. well clone of you.<br /> <br /> This also runs into the army of Exalted problem.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough the idea of being able to produce familiars out of your heart's blood that you can remerge with like some forms of Hugin and Mugin seems fine to me. Again just go with the idea while USEFUL these things are damned vulnerable or risk becoming rampant/independent. You being a lunar can play and manipulate life but life is still life and its always striving for self. This also creates a distinction from the Green Sun Princes OR the Abyssals with their version of minion-mancy. Abyssals are necromancers summoning undead horrors and demons are a Devil-Tiger's new external organs or sybiotic lifeforms. A lunar can't create a full being and make it a convenient slave it at the least is a pet if not more.<br /> BTW for that send out a familiar thing while it can be killed if you can eat it (or whatever at it) you get the benefits of remerging and learning what it did or experienced.<br /> <br /> I suppose that is a little monstrous.<br /> <br /> I guess I lean to giving Lunars powerful versatile tools but not solutions. the issue is this might have some problem fitting in attributes or the right tree.<br /> <br /> I didn't think of the duplicate things you are wearing issue. Maybe only mundane things? I'm okay with that as a munition work around. For one it means timing for when to clone matters. Also no matter what someone is going empty to supply the Lunar. And again if they are a lifeform, not just an illusion or projection this will cause trouble. There is backing up your fellow soldier and then there is the guy who skives your ammo and leaves you empty underfire as an intention of his strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T21:13:19-07:00","id":1097971,"title":"","content":"I know it was a 2e charm, but that Adorjan one that let you close yourself, but the clone didn't have any of your powers and was basically mortal seems like it should still be a valid design paradigm, if you want to have a longer term clone than just making a momentary copy out of your shadow or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:41:55-07:00","id":1098064,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's necessarily wise or practical to extrapolate things about Lunar charm-set abilities based on an individual Solar charm.<br /> <br /> Really, this is one of the best things that the move to 3rd edition granted; it opened up a creative space in the game to indicate that merely the existence of a charm does not indicate space in the game that the rest of the essence using individuals (for lack of a better term) should be judged around.<br /> <br /> Or, more practically, I just don't think it's a very useful thought exercise to consider Solar &quot;clone effect&quot; charm affects the game world, or how the Lunar would/could accomplish the same feat, or what other ways the Lunar may do so. The Lunar may develop many different ways of expressing the one as many / I'm a battle group kind of power. For that matter, there may be other ways for the Solar to express that sort of ability outside of Athletics, especially when one factors in the presence of unique post-E6 powers which (happily) are treated less like individual cogs within the complete Solar charm set and more like unique powers grown from the individual expression of that single individual who developed them. I'd further assume that this is how all Exalted high-essence powers function, especially since 3rd edition is so much more forgiving in terms of how a given power could be expressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:35:31-07:00","id":1098075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination#post1097768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also a big part of the reason the Lunar Exalted cannot have anything approximating Phantom-Conjuring Performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worst Masters of Illusions, ever.<br /> <br /> (Not that they ever were, it's just a funny contrast to me).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination#post1097768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Exalted have never had an effect quite like Glorious Solar Saber, because a Dexterity Charm tree doesn't impose the same limitations as a Melee Charm tree. It is not appropriate for the Lunar Exalted to have a Green Lantern power which allows them to conjure any object or tool they might need, the way that Infernal Exalted could with the Charms of She Who Lives In Her Name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I'm being dumb here, but doesn't this imply that Lunars never have combat charms ever? If you can't have a specialised &quot;summon artefact&quot; Charm for combat, because all their Charms have to be general to Dex, then how do they have any combat specialised Dex Charms at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:57:19-07:00","id":1098129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098075#post1098075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I'm being dumb here, but doesn't this imply that Lunars never have combat charms ever? If you can't have a specialised &quot;summon artefact&quot; Charm for combat, because all their Charms have to be general to Dex, then how do they have any combat specialised Dex Charms at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're confusing &quot;the limitations of a single Charm within a set&quot; with &quot;the limitations of ALL Charms within a set&quot;.<br /> <br /> A single Solar Melee Charm generally only focuses on offense or defense, and only one trick thereof. Every Solar Melee Charm before and after it likewise must generally be strictly offensive or defensive. More importantly, all of these Solar Melee Charms must relate to the Melee Ability, which is why Glorious Solar Saber cannot serve as the basis for Immaculate Golden Bow or Words-as-Workshop Method.<br /> <br /> A Dexterity Charm set has no Ability-related restrictions. If the Lunar Exalted could have Charms that fashioned artifact-quality tools out of Essence, then Glorious Lunar Saber, Immaculate Silver Bow, or Howls-as-Workshop Method could all be found in the same Attribute. Sooner or later, that broadness eliminates the restrictions that keep this capability from evolving into a &quot;Green Lantern Ring&quot; power that lets the Lunar Exalted act like Infernals with the Charms of She Who Lives In Her Name, creating walls and constructs of Essence to fight telekinetically at a distance without needing to use weapons or animal forms.<br /> <br /> This is also why the free-form holographic powers of Phantom-Conjuring Technique are inappropriate for the Lunar Exalted. Such an external power renders their powers of internal transformation redundant and meaningless.<br /> <br /> All of the other Exalted have already got &quot;external manipulation of the world&quot; well-covered, between Solar mastery, Terrestrial elementalism, Sidereal cheats, Getimian hacks, Abyssal blasphemies, and Infernal heresies.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are being parred down to focus on an intensely personal sort of mastery, with some extraneous parts of that internal focus being cut off and given to the Liminal Exalted who can expand upon those pieces in ways that were never appropriate for the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alchemical Dexterity is different. For one thing, the Chosen of the Machine God should naturally be good with any kind of tools. But there's also the fact that they can only load so many Charms at a time, which limits how broad their powers can be at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-29-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:04:31-07:00","id":1098132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098064#post1098064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's necessarily wise or practical to extrapolate things about Lunar charm-set abilities based on an individual Solar charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, then address the <i>other questions</i>.<br /> <br /> Do you think that, if Lunar Charms can clone themselves for distractions when dodging or for more damage with Decisive attacks, they should be able to clone their armor and daiklaves too, or must they often clone themselves with animal forms so that nakedness doesn't give the real Lunar away?<br /> <br /> So many complaints about &quot;don't copy the Solars!&quot; but it doesn't feel like any of you are confronting the real issues that might set Lunar magic apart from Solar magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:54:56-07:00","id":1098151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098129#post1098129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A single Solar Melee Charm generally only focuses on offense or defense, and only one trick thereof. Every Solar Melee Charm before and after it likewise must generally be strictly offensive or defensive. More importantly, all of these Solar Melee Charms must relate to the Melee Ability, which is why Glorious Solar Saber cannot serve as the basis for Immaculate Golden Bow or Words-as-Workshop Method.<br /> <br /> A Dexterity Charm set has no Ability-related restrictions. If the Lunar Exalted could have Charms that fashioned artifact-quality tools out of Essence, then Glorious Lunar Saber, Immaculate Silver Bow, or Howls-as-Workshop Method could all be found in the same Attribute. Sooner or later, that broadness eliminates the restrictions that keep this capability from evolving into a &quot;Green Lantern Ring&quot; power that lets the Lunar Exalted act like Infernals with the Charms of She Who Lives In Her Name, creating walls and constructs of Essence to fight telekinetically at a distance without needing to use weapons or animal forms..</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, well, I'm not so sure that this all follows tbh. I don't really quite get how we get from &quot;If a Lunar could forge a sword from the essence of anima and speed, then he could forge a bow, then of course, Lunar telekenesis and force fields. And so because no Lunar telekenesis and force fields, no sword.&quot;. Does this seem a logically necessary progression to any third party posting here? (Sincerely, this isn't just to be a jerk, I'd like some to tell me if I'm crazy and not getting something obvious, or that I'm not crazy and it's not obvious. I've read it a few times and it's not clicking.)<br /> <br /> In at least one sense, it doesn't make sense to me that Solar Melee would build in a way that means the user has to remain using Melee, but that Lunar Dexterity could build in a way the obviates the character actually performing physically dexterous actions. Which is what telekenesis would do? You're not going to get telekenesis because that is not an expression of physical Dexterity but replaces and competes with it. But I will bow out here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:54:07-07:00","id":1098172,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the simpler truths, the Lunar Exalted have NEVER had anything like Glorious Solar Saber or Phantom Conjuring Technique, and the developer comments about their internal focus and &quot;no illusions&quot; make it pretty clear that 3rd Edition isn't going to change that.<br /> <br /> So, ADDRESS THE QUESTION, please.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you think that, if Lunar Charms can clone themselves for distractions when dodging or for more damage with Decisive attacks, they should be able to clone their armor and daiklaves too, or must they often clone themselves with animal forms so that nakedness doesn't give the real Lunar away?&quot;<br /> <br /> Are any of you here only because you feel &quot;someone is wrong on the internet&quot;, or does the subject actually inspire a curiosity in you?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:35:38-07:00","id":1098188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098172#post1098172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the simpler truths, the Lunar Exalted have NEVER had anything like Glorious Solar Saber or Phantom Conjuring Technique, and the developer comments about their internal focus and &quot;no illusions&quot; make it pretty clear that 3rd Edition isn't going to change that.<br /> <br /> So, ADDRESS THE QUESTION, please.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you think that, if Lunar Charms can clone themselves for distractions when dodging or for more damage with Decisive attacks, they should be able to clone their armor and daiklaves too, or must they often clone themselves with animal forms so that nakedness doesn't give the real Lunar away?&quot;<br /> <br /> Are any of you here only because you feel &quot;someone is wrong on the internet&quot;, or does the subject actually inspire a curiosity in you?</div> </div> </div> </div>First. I don't know if you're actually angry but you are coming off as very aggressive. Please see if you can measure your words. Everyone here cares about this and we all know how dedicated you are. I just don't think that you're expressing yourself a very welcoming manner.<br /> <br /> But you are right let's focus on the actual question and not get bound down by the distraction<br /> <br /> Personally I'm fine with them copying all Mortal equipment. Even luxurious items. For one you create more complications if you duplicate the exact same dress time and time and time again.<br /> <br /> If it is something exceptional, even if it technically isn't an artifact object such as relatively mundane magic item or powder or something. . . just a steal my idea about a surcharge of difference of special items that are exceptionally unique. Say they require a mote surcharge of the difference between zero and whatever their value will be<br /> Otherwise they go uncopied on the clone.<br /> <br /> This also justifies lunars being relatively low in terms of armament; clothing; or other aesthetics which can feed back into their sort of fantasy Barbarian thing<br /> <br /> Mainly that's for their swarm charm or series of charms. If they still keep their versatile pocket space abilities then I would totally let them be able to be cloned and wind up with a set of armor and arms Erza meets Naruto Style.<br /> <br /> Inherent drawback being once it's out of your pocket space- well it's out of your pocket space. It is not duplicated and you can not switch after you do the set. Or at least not the instantaneous summon way unless you have a Charm for that or something<br /> <br /> What are some problems with my proposal? all of this is pure theorycraft not a lot of practical experience here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 05-29-2017, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:51:24-07:00","id":1098250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097908#post1097908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you understand that my idea of clone is appearance agnostic, and that I'm very much envisioning a Lunar becoming a battle group of animals?<br /> <br /> I even talked about how the Lunar Exalted might not be able to effectively use their natural human forms in this manner, since in that case their human-form clones would likely be naked and unarmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always just sort of figured a Lunar in that sort of situation would just turn into a giant bear, or rip a tree out of the ground and wield it as an improvised club.<br /> <br /> [lunar elder rant] I mean, what's the world coming to if a new Lunar can't rip a tree out of the ground with her bare hands, for Luna's Sake. None of that &quot;sword&quot; nonsense. Back in my day, we used whole yeddim as weapons and by Sol we liked it! [/lunar elder rant]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T15:28:16-07:00","id":1098258,"title":"","content":"Well in Game terms it doesn't work. Like how animals fall into a memory whole in lore discussion despite they would be the Creation wide version of machines and electronics. The stats are so pitiful. Also its ineffecient. To do that you lose your mana points. Finally it makes them look like naked rednecks at the Prom. Every other splat gets cool mythic super weapons. Tehy should too.<br /> <br /> This is especially when Sidereals and Terrestrials, their likely antagonists, seem to be cleaning gear out of their seat cushions that completely negates the much lamented &quot;limited powers&quot; they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:02:30-07:00","id":1098312,"title":"","content":"It just occurred to me that &quot;I temporarily split off a (quickly fading) clone&quot; might be a Lunar approach to an effect similar to Lightning Strikes Twice (from Solar Brawl), with the Lunar splitting off as they attack, and the clone then performing the second attack. This might require them to be able to copy their gear, at least for a few moments, though.<br /> <br /> I mean, apparently Lunars might be getting King Cuerno's &quot;Arrow from the Depths of Hell&quot; as a Charm to launch themselves at their opponents. I could see that propelling the foe away sort of like Heaven Thunder Hammer. Meanwhile the clone is running off to give them another blow at the point of impact or drawing an actual arrow to shoot them as they fly away, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:56:37-07:00","id":1098325,"title":"","content":"That's not even accounting for 3rd Edition's version of Beast Spirit Defense, which would likely be a Clash attack rather than a perfect parry, and involves throwing your anima at someone in the form of your totemic beast.<br /> <br /> Where a Solar spends their anima to make a second attack with Iron Peony Blossom, a Lunar might just throw their anima at someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T03:51:27-07:00","id":1098388,"title":"","content":"I would personally not have any issue with a Lunar Charm like this having all of the copies being equipped in the same manner, and also looking like the Lunar.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm all for the shapeshifting, but I think Lunars still need a heavy does of clever trickster and elevated prowess Charms. Not to prove any kind of point about them not being zoo Exalted or anything, just because I think it's a cosmetic that is natural to Lunars. I think a big part of distinguishing Lunars from Solars is going to need to be about how their Charms <i>interact</i> rather than just what they do individually.<br /> <br /> I mean, we've got more elemental kinds of Dragon Blooded Charms now, but we've still got Charms that are basically just doing a thing while referencing the element metaphorically, but they still play into differences in how the Dragon Blooded function because of the elemental Keywords and the aura mechanic.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, I would not consider some things that function off of illusions to be out of place, while no more making the Lunars illusionist Exalted than the Solars having Phantom-Conjuring Performance makes them illusionists.<br /> <br /> \u200bBack to the cloning, I think their weapons would be evenly distributed regardless of an inability to conjure a new weapon individually, because I don't think the Charms of anybody should be constructed according to that logic. It's the same as how a Solar being able to evoke a magic weapon from their spirit doesn't equate to being able to shape objects in general from sunlight and soul stuff, because the magic doesn't have a reductive element; there isn't an element that you can break down and reorganize to do something different, it's a capability that arises from a singular purpose informed by a narrative and erroneous human perception and categorization.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo a Lunar trickster power of making a hoard of copies can also copy one's weapon because it's going with a narrative of making the copies, while they lack a narrative of evoking a weapon from their spirits like that, and there's no contradiction because these things aren't connected in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I'm not saying that this would be terminology that would be recognised or used in character, I'm just using it as a basis to describe how one might write magic here, and how it tends to end up being written almost everywhere)<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know if this answers any specific questions that have been asked, but it's my perspective on a broad read of this subject. I hope that it's useful, or at least relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:22:45-07:00","id":1098397,"title":"","content":"I certainly agree with you Isator. A couple of things to note:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'm all for the shapeshifting, but I think Lunars still need a heavy does of clever trickster and elevated prowess Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2nd ed Lunar charmset was quite dull; very Silver Solar (though with a few particular charms that players enjoyed as being more distinct). My Lunar was very shapeshifting-focused, because it was more fun than their actual charms; but I wouldn't want everything they had to be about shapeshifting. For one thing, there's a limit to what you can do with shapeshifting (I found, for example, that once I could turn into a tyrant lizard, it seemed a waste of time to get more combat shapeshifting), but also, you just want to be able to do more than that.<br /> Shapeshifting is good for some stuff, but not so much for others. The other Lunar in the game (and this was a pretty high essence game, so we had about 40+ charms each) was a social Lunar; shapeshifting was certainly not the solution to everything that character wanted to do. Her player had a lot of fun using the charms that inflicted lust or fear on people, or bound them to their social unit/turned them against it.<br /> So yeah, clever trickster charms.<br /> Elevated prowess is fine too; I think the issue was that half (well, more than half) of the Lunars charms in 2nd ed were that. I don't think they should be entirely eliminated, or all forced to become shapeshifting charms as if Lunars can't just be really charismatic or strong or whatever; they just need to be a supporting part of the Lunar charmset, rather than the bulk of it.<br /> <br /> The point is, while I'd like to see more shapeshifting in the Lunar set, I'd also like to see other stuff.<br /> <br /> One thing I also bought into besides Lunar shapeshifting, was the odd shaman-esque and mystical charms (as did a few of the other Lunar PCs). They were very appropriate for a No Moon; and they're not something Solars can do. Unfortunately, however, there just really weren't many of them written up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, we've got more elemental kinds of Dragon Blooded Charms now, but we've still got Charms that are basically just doing a thing while referencing the element metaphorically, but they still play into differences in how the Dragon Blooded function because of the elemental Keywords and the aura mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I think, is probably quite an important point, but I'm not really sure how much we can say about it without a better understanding of what a 3rd ed Lunar charmset would look like. What I mean is; I think the DB comparison is probably a good one, in the sense that DB charms might just be enhanced prowess, but still fit into the charmset's unique magic in terms of their elemental associations, etc. Which could also perhaps work with Lunars, making their prowess enhancers feel distinct both thematically and mechanically... but I have no idea how, essentially.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I would not consider some things that function off of illusions to be out of place, while no more making the Lunars illusionist Exalted than the Solars having Phantom-Conjuring Performance makes them illusionists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I never got what the massive issue with Lunar illusion charms was. I felt it was fine for moon-blessed tricksters and shamans. Perhaps Terrifying Argent Witches, which was very illusion-based IIRC, turned people off it. But I don't at all see the issue with a few illusion magicks amongst their charmset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Do you think that, if Lunar Charms can clone themselves for distractions when dodging or for more damage with Decisive attacks, they should be able to clone their armor and daiklaves too, or must they often clone themselves with animal forms so that nakedness doesn't give the real Lunar away?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit complex I think; essentially, I've got no great problem with their clones having clothes, or the same equipment, in the middle of a battle. But I can well imagine PCs trying to abuse it to produce more daiklaives, essentially, which wouldn't be apprpropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-30-2017, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:41:53-07:00","id":1098400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098397#post1098397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Yeah, I never got what the massive issue with Lunar illusion charms was. I felt it was fine for moon-blessed tricksters and shamans. Perhaps Terrifying Argent Witches, which was very illusion-based IIRC, turned people off it. But I don't at all see the issue with a few illusion magicks amongst their charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think it's a case of some people reading a comment on how Lunars won't be specifically illusionists as either implying a statement of having no illusions, or an insistence that there be no illusions for it to be consistently realised.<br /> <br /> \u200bConversely, you get people who became very attached to references to Lunar illusions in the First Edition core for a variety of reasons, and it becomes their example for the question of the ever elusive Lunar identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:47:43-07:00","id":1098401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098258#post1098258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in Game terms it doesn't work. Like how animals fall into a memory whole in lore discussion despite they would be the Creation wide version of machines and electronics. The stats are so pitiful. Also its ineffecient. To do that you lose your mana points. Finally it makes them look like naked rednecks at the Prom. Every other splat gets cool mythic super weapons. Tehy should too.<br /> <br /> This is especially when Sidereals and Terrestrials, their likely antagonists, seem to be cleaning gear out of their seat cushions that completely negates the much lamented &quot;limited powers&quot; they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like a Lunar's essence is power flowing from within; and, that every Lunar should know deep down that the most deadly weapon they possess is themselves. It's not that they can't use weapons, or that they shouldn't, it's just that a weapon for a lunar is not the actual focus of their power- it's just a conduit for their terrifying monster strengthen or dreadful lightning quickness.<br /> <br /> A Lunar doesn't beat you because she has a magic sword. She beats you because she's a Lunar. The sword helps, but anything would work almost as well. I feel like Lunars should certainly have charms that allow them to treat anything they find laying around as if it were an artifact weapon, if they so choose.<br /> <br /> I personally don't think it'd be athematic for a Lunar to be able to make a bunch of clones of themselves with all their stuff. Depending on if you count the Handsome Monkey King as a Solar or Lunar influence, it makes perfect sense thematically. I like trickster! Lunar things with a passion, but I don't feel like a Lunar would be as intimidated about having to fight without anything on hand as, say, a Solar.<br /> <br /> Because if you dropped a naked, unarmed Solar on a deserted island filled with hostile dinosaurs or something, he'd probably set up a crude smithy out of a few rocks and the like and forge for himself a magnificent set of armor and a sword fit for kings, then lay waste to the wildlife with his amazing martial prowess and carefully honed mastery of the sword.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can just rip a tree out of the ground and stride forth confident in the knowledge that they need literally nothing else to destroy a tyrant lizard. They could, in fact, do so just as well with their bare hands.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:19:05-07:00","id":1098755,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused by some of the premises of the OP... <br /> <br /> Is the assertion that Lunars gave no Glorious Solar Saber Charm specifically a reference to the concept of creating weapons? Because the purpose of Glorious Solar Saber is to give you an artifact quality weapon to use, if I remember right, and Lunars did have an equivalent with Claws of the Silver Moon which grants the Lunar artifact equivalent weapons from all of their unarmed options. <br /> <br /> If it's specifically about creating a handheld weapon... Didn't Lunars have a Charm that lets them create weaponry from their environment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:57:56-07:00","id":1098764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098755#post1098755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused by some of the premises of the OP...<br /> <br /> Is the assertion that Lunars gave no Glorious Solar Saber Charm specifically a reference to the concept of creating weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Because the entire first post is framed as talking about clothes and hand-held weapons and questioning whether Lunar Exalted can create anything but naked clones. Whether or not any of those clones could employ Artifact-quality fangs is completely beside the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's specifically about creating a handheld weapon... Didn't Lunars have a Charm that lets them create weaponry from their environment? </div> </div> </div>They <i>did</i>, but they likely <i>won't</i> from now on, because 3rd Edition Lunar Exalted allegedly rely more on changing themselves than changing the world around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:15:47-07:00","id":1098775,"title":"","content":"I think it's possible to get a bit too caught up on fangs and claws.<br /> Lunars have a powerful connection to one of the Five Magic Materials so while using uprooted trees as clubs and claws like wolverine may seem evocative they shouldn't be the last words on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T09:16:03-07:00","id":1098794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098764#post1098764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Because the entire first post is framed as talking about clothes and hand-held weapons and questioning whether Lunar Exalted can create anything but naked clones. Whether or not any of those clones could employ Artifact-quality fangs is completely beside the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They <i>did</i>, but they likely <i>won't</i> from now on, because 3rd Edition Lunar Exalted allegedly rely more on changing themselves than changing the world around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... &quot;rely more on&quot; is not an exclusionary statement, just an indicator of preference. So, there has been established precedence for Lunars being able to use their powers regarding objects which are non-magical in nature. <br /> <br /> I think there's a big question that has to be considered as to what the impact of these clones is meant to be. What's the purpose being accomplished? Are they distractions? Can they use similar powers as the Lunar themself? <br /> <br /> Maybe the categorical capability of making clones can have different effects when used for different purposes? For example, clones created as a distraction can be more numerous/weaker but serve their purpose less if they're incapable of being deceptive. Whereas clones created as a threat in of themselves must be stronger and more capable of tapping into the Lunar's capabilities in order to achieve being a threat in of themselves, in which case deception isn't the intended goal there. <br /> <br /> I can't say that Lunars should only have one option here... A warrior Lunar that can be a dangerous pack of wolves should be just as viable as a trickster Lunar that confuses their opponent by deceiving them as to which target is the real threat, which requires appearing as the Lunar. <br /> <br /> It's a poor shapeshifter/trickster that can't pull off a deception simply because they lack the props to sell it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T10:19:30-07:00","id":1098813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098794#post1098794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... &quot;rely more on&quot; is not an exclusionary statement, just an indicator of preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers felt so strongly about limiting the transformative properties of moonsilver that they made it the only magical material with words devoting to talking about what it <i>explicitly couldn't</i> do, rather than relying on the implications formed by the things it could.<br /> <br /> The fear seems to be that if they give an inch (moonsilver can transform for some Evocations) then gamers would take a mile (moonsilver can trivially become any possible weapon).<br /> <br /> If the Lunar Exalted can produce copies of artifact armor and weaponry for a battle-group's worth of clones to use in battle, then what limits them from having Glorious Lunar Saber?<br /> <br /> If the Lunar can produce mere illusions of equipment for brief-lived distraction clones, then what limits the Lunar Exalted from having the illusion Charms that Holden and Morke insistently said they would not have?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, there has been established precedence for Lunars being able to use their powers regarding objects which are non-magical in nature. </div> </div> </div>Not in this Edition.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at previous Editions, there's established precedent for Lunar Exalted being able to warp the laws of space and time, too. But now that's for the Getimian Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's a big question that has to be considered as to what the impact of these clones is meant to be. What's the purpose being accomplished? Are they distractions? </div> </div> </div>Momentary clones could be used for distractions, whether for dodging and ducking behind cover to hide, or for making an attack from an unexpected angle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they use similar powers as the Lunar themself? </div> </div> </div>Brief distractions wouldn't, because such brief clones are just fluff justifications for the effects of the true Lunar's action.<br /> <br /> More durable clones used to fill out a battle-group would be using the Lunar's own powers to keep up with him. If he's going to use a movement Charm, they're all going to use the same movement Charm.<br /> <br /> If the Lunar Exalted can produce copies of artifact armor and weaponry for a battle-group's worth of clones to use in battle, then what limits the Lunar Exalted from having Glorious Lunar Saber?<br /> <br /> If the Lunar can produce mere illusions of equipment for brief-lived distraction clones, then what limits the Lunar Exalted from having the illusion Charms that Holden and Morke insistently said they would not have?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> clones created as a distraction can be more numerous/weaker but serve their purpose less if they're incapable of being deceptive. </div> </div> </div>They're extremely capable of being deceptive as animals if the Lunar is the same species of animal, or if all of them are a different species than the one the Lunar was just a moment ago. No clothes or weapons are needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a poor shapeshifter/trickster that can't pull off a deception simply because they lack the props to sell it. </div> </div> </div>You assume they need props to sell it.<br /> <br /> Holden and Morke said they'd be plenty tricksy and deceptive even without illusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T10:22:11-07:00","id":1098814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098775#post1098775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's possible to get a bit too caught up on fangs and claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when I make threads like this, I'm stuck between a rock and hard place.<br /> <br /> If I advocate that the Lunars get something like Glorious Lunar Saber, I would be laughed at by half the forum. If I try to acknowledge and work within the idea that Lunar Exalted won't get any such Charm, the other half of the forum challenges that very idea.<br /> <br /> I can't win either way, even when I try to take a neutral approach and merely ask for opinions. Someone finds something else to complain about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:20:50-07:00","id":1098839,"title":"","content":"... Wait what? Now you're talking about artifacts? And correlating Lunars and Moonsilver as if they're the same thing? And arguing statements from previous Developers as if Minton and Vance have no say? <br /> <br /> Okay, look Sunder the Gold, I'm good with talking about speculation, about theorizing and debating thematics, and even about discussing preferences with what either of us would like to see in the future. <br /> <br /> I don't see you asking for opinions here. If you were, I don't think you'd be replying with assertions about Holden and Morke. That's just a tactic to beat someone down. <br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure what you're really looking for here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:21:50-07:00","id":1099002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097782#post1097782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm not too sold on examining Faster Than Self to construct one's model for an equivalent Lunar Charm, especially since having it be unable to clone equipment will just lead to more &quot;Silver Solar&quot; mentality. Might be better to just blaze a new trail entirely, even if it gets to the same place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that you also think that Lunar Charms would be incapable of simply conjuring up weapons for themselves, and copies of existing weapons for their clones to use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T21:11:48-07:00","id":1099011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098388#post1098388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally not have any issue with a Lunar Charm like this having all of the copies being equipped in the same manner, and also looking like the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you think Ma-Ha-Suchi could split into a battle-group where every clone of himself held a clone of Corpse Drill, or just something that looked like Corpse Drill?<br /> <br /> Let's suppose the the copy spears are only functionally mortal spears. That's still Ma-Ha-Suchi producing dozens of functional spears as well as clones. Do you think he could make the spear copies without the clones?<br /> <br /> Would it be just a straight port of Glorious Lunar Saber, or limited to producing weapons only of the mundane level?<br /> <br /> If there are no functional spears at all, but merely the illusion of spears, what are the limits to the illusions that Lunar Exalted can create? If spears, then clothes? If clothes, then disguises? If they can create illusionary disguises, then do they have any need for Shaping The Ideal Form for making lasting changes to their actual faces and genders?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI'm all for the shapeshifting, but I think Lunars still need a heavy does of clever trickster and elevated prowess Charms. </div> </div> </div>So do I. But when I try to explore these things, people say, &quot;Too Silver Solar&quot;, so I'm trying to explore uniquely Lunar tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, we've got more elemental kinds of Dragon Blooded Charms now, but we've still got Charms that are basically just doing a thing while referencing the element metaphorically, but they still play into differences in how the Dragon Blooded function because of the elemental Keywords and the aura mechanic. </div> </div> </div>But for Lunar Exalted, it's shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Lunar rush-oriented Charms will likely prominently feature a Charm to flurry a rush action together with an action to shapeshift into a form suitable for pursuit. Charms for flurrying shapeshifting actions with disengage (turn into a bird to fly away), withdraw or contest of speed (turn into a cheetah to run as fast as possible), re-establish surprise (turn into something small)...<br /> <br /> There's also their Rage and (Solar) Bond themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T21:18:19-07:00","id":1099013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098397#post1098397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit complex I think; essentially, I've got no great problem with their clones having clothes, or the same equipment, in the middle of a battle. But I can well imagine PCs trying to abuse it to produce more daiklaives, essentially, which wouldn't be apprpropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it makes sense that when a Lunar clone dies, it just disappears, along with any copies of your equipment it might have.<br /> <br /> As I said, this would prevent a Lunar from forming a textile business just by copying a few expensive dresses hundreds of times.<br /> <br /> Copies of artifact weapons can also simply disappear. Further, HAVING a hundred copies of Islebreaker wouldn't mechanically give Leviathan much of an advantage, since it probably wouldn't directly increase the power of Islebreaker's Evocations.<br /> <br /> As I try to point out, if Leviathan could make a temporary copy of Islebreaker as well as a temporary copy of himself, then what stops him from making temporary dire-lances alone, without any clones, so that he can use the temporary dire-lance himself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:41:31-07:00","id":1099038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099013#post1099013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I try to point out, if Leviathan could make a temporary copy of Islebreaker as well as a temporary copy of himself, then what stops him from making temporary dire-lances alone, without any clones, so that he can use the temporary dire-lance himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>At a guess, because it just doesn't work that way?<br /> <br /> A sorcerer slinging Rain of Doom probably wants his buddy two range bands away to not be caught in it, but that's just not how the spell works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T00:56:15-07:00","id":1099050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099011#post1099011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think he could make the spear copies without the clones?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr at least, not the way that you're saying. Possibly something like a Manipulation Charm that allows one to &quot;copy&quot; their weapon or anybody else's for some eventual purpose of tricking another. A thief gets to think that prior to the fight, they stole your sacred weapon, but then you reveal that your sacred weapon has been in your storage chest all along, and what they're holding disintegrates or turns out to be a rubber chicken.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith Charms, as I think with most magic of this type, form follow function. There isn't an independent capacity to copy or create things for which one finds multiple applications; there is a mythic purpose, and a process that fulfils it.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike I said, it's the same as how Glorious Solar Saber does not mean that Solars can conjure absolutely anything, because it's not about shaping hard light being applied to a function, it's about the mythic warrior being able to draw a weapon from within themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:33:15-07:00","id":1099065,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think for mythic warriors, there's a reliance on mythic themes; the Lunar can copy himself (via illusions or actual spawning; one is likely much higher level than the other) and the copies have copies of his weapons (which, I think, should only last as long as the clone, and maybe should fall apart if removed from the clone), because that's part of the theme, but that doesn't mean the Lunar should just be able to copy the weapon itself. I think that's okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> How many clones are we talking? How long do they last? Are they real or illusory? How does this work mechanically? I know these questions have come up already, but I think it depends a lot on that.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel like if the Lunar is making himself into a battle-group for one scene, then it's fine, but if he's growing a clone of himself for general purposes, and the clone is going to last a while (until decommited or killed, for example), then that guy/girl should be naked, or at most just wearing clothes and that's it, not armed. That may seem odd, but there's an element of what's practical for the game; it's awkward if 10 days later you've still got extra swords, but it's also awkward if you split up in the middle of combat and your clones are not armed.<br /> As you said, when they die the copies should definitely vanish, but I think that's still potentially too long, and starts getting into abusable territory. But one scene is fine.<br /> <br /> You know, thinking about it, I feel much, much more comfortable with the image of a Lunar splitting into 10 versions, and his moonsilver sword splitting into 10 copies, than I do with a jade or orichalcum sword splitting into 10 copies.<br /> <br /> The other thing I find myself thinking, with this conversation, is that the more we talk about it, the more I'm quite happy for Lunars to turn into swarms of rats or bees or whatever (which I absolutely want them to be able to do), than be able to turn into a swarm of clones to become a battle group. I don't hate the idea, but nor do I find myself that interested in it. I wouldn't hate Lunars being able to do it, but I'm not sure it's a charm I'd want; being able to turn into a swarm of animals is fine enough.<br /> Though I do like the idea of spawning 1 or 2 clones for general utility (probably as quite a high-essence charm though, like 4 or 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-01-2017, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T03:28:09-07:00","id":1099091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099065#post1099065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(via illusions or actual spawning; one is likely much higher level than the other)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf they're both still able to hit people, I think the distinction might be arbitrary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T04:53:53-07:00","id":1099115,"title":"","content":"I was assuming that illusory Lunars stabbing you with illusory daiklaives would be less deadly than actual Lunar clones with actual copies of daiklaives. Similarly, I was assuming they wouldn't be able to pick things up, carry things, etc, not to mention being less able to take independent action, and thus overall be less useful.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yes, the distinction wouldn't matter that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:20:25-07:00","id":1099181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099038#post1099038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a guess, because it just doesn't work that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>A possibility <i>did</i> occur to me.<br /> <br /> What if the Lunar can only clone something he already has available? His clones have his clothes and weapons, but if he were naked and empty-handed, so to would be his clones.<br /> <br /> He can't copy unattuned artifacts, either, and also nothing he cannot hold or wear. Any burden that could be described as &quot;carry&quot; rather than &quot;hold&quot; cannot be copied.<br /> <br /> This equips a Lunar's distracting and enduring clones while keeping the Lunar from creating stuff out of nothing. And of course, all of the cloned equipment disappears when the clones do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:56:41-07:00","id":1099218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099181#post1099181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Lunar can only clone something he already has available?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda something I was just implicitly assuming; a Lunar who makes a clone of &quot;myself who has the Aidenweiss,&quot; or the Eye of Autochthon, or that wedding band from MoEP:Infernals is gonna get shenanigans called on him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099181#post1099181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His clones have his clothes and weapons, but if he were naked and empty-handed, so to would be his clones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure - if you're trying to keep potential attackers in the dark as to which you is the <i>real</i> you, having your clones dress differently than you would be counterproductive, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099181#post1099181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He can't copy unattuned artifacts, either, and also nothing he cannot hold or wear. Any burden that could be described as &quot;carry&quot; rather than &quot;hold&quot; cannot be copied.</div> </div> </div> </div>This produced in my head a mental image of a Lunar player trying to convince the ST to permit him to clone the Imperial Manse, at which point the ST called Rocks Fall, Everyone Dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-01-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T11:26:38-07:00","id":1099223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099218#post1099218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kinda something I was just implicitly assuming; a Lunar who makes a clone of &amp;quot;myself who has the Aidenweiss,&amp;quot; or the Eye of Autochthon, or that wedding band from MoEP:Infernals is gonna get shenanigans called on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that the Lunar could only do something like Glorious Lunar Saber to copy something he already has, rather than make something he doesn't. And he wouldn't use it outside of cloning because would be little point to multiplying Islebreaker when you don't have a clone to use it and no one else could use it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure - if you're trying to keep potential attackers in the dark as to which you is the <i>real</i> you, having your clones dress differently than you would be counterproductive, wouldn't it? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but we're talking about what is permissible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This produced in my head a mental image of a Lunar player trying to convince the ST to permit him to clone the Imperial Manse, at which point the ST called Rocks Fall, Everyone Dies. </div> </div> </div>Hah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T11:32:07-07:00","id":1099224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099223#post1099223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that the Lunar could only do something like Glorious Lunar Saber to copy something he already has, rather than make something he doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, I don't think the Eye of Autochthon or the Aidenweiss are presently in the hands of Lunars, hence my using them as examples.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:05:56-07:00","id":1099253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098312#post1098312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just occurred to me that &quot;I temporarily split off a (quickly fading) clone&quot; might be a Lunar approach to an effect similar to Lightning Strikes Twice (from Solar Brawl), with the Lunar splitting off as they attack, and the clone then performing the second attack. This might require them to be able to copy their gear, at least for a few moments, though.<br /> <br /> I mean, apparently Lunars might be getting King Cuerno's &quot;Arrow from the Depths of Hell&quot; as a Charm to launch themselves at their opponents. I could see that propelling the foe away sort of like Heaven Thunder Hammer. Meanwhile the clone is running off to give them another blow at the point of impact or drawing an actual arrow to shoot them as they fly away, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms that let a Lunar punch someone a mile away and then leap a whole mile in order to hit them again strike me as Strength-based, actually.<br /> <br /> Though I'd like to try working clones or anima-born totems in, somehow, rather than just copying the Solar Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:28:33-07:00","id":1099263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099181#post1099181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possibility <i>did</i> occur to me.<br /> <br /> What if the Lunar can only clone something he already has available? His clones have his clothes and weapons, but if he were naked and empty-handed, so to would be his clones.<br /> <br /> He can't copy unattuned artifacts, either, and also nothing he cannot hold or wear. Any burden that could be described as &quot;carry&quot; rather than &quot;hold&quot; cannot be copied.<br /> <br /> This equips a Lunar's distracting and enduring clones while keeping the Lunar from creating stuff out of nothing. And of course, all of the cloned equipment disappears when the clones do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Alucard, I was assuming all of these to be the case anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T15:48:28-07:00","id":1099671,"title":"","content":"Taking the idea further...<br /> <br /> What if a Lunar <i>could</i> learn how to duplicate the weapons they already have on them, without the clones? Sometimes, that's handy.<br /> <br /> <i>Twin Fang Technique.</i> As long as the Lunar maintains a hold on the original sword, he can create a duplicate to use in his other hand. This could let him enjoy the Clash bonus of paired weapons, or else employ certain other Charms, such as those of Steel Devil Style<br /> <br /> It might also allow the Lunar to extend his supply of ammunition. As long as he holds a throwing spear in one hand or a throwing dagger in his pocket, he can hurl clones of the weapon at his opponents.<br /> <br /> This could lead to 3rd Edition versions of 1st Edition Charms like &quot;Silver Waterfall Technique&quot; or &quot;Rain of Feathered Doom&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T16:10:53-07:00","id":1099675,"title":"","content":"Well... yeah, it's useful, but it just seems unthematic for a Lunar charm.<br /> It'd fine as a Moonsilver evocation though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:05:29-07:00","id":1099687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099675#post1099675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... yeah, it's useful, but it just seems unthematic for a Lunar charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've already argued that Lunar Exalted can clone equipment together with clones; why does it suddenly become unthematic without a clone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:30:10-07:00","id":1099693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099687#post1099687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've already argued that Lunar Exalted can clone equipment together with clones; why does it suddenly become unthematic without a clone?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just playing devil's advocate here\u2026)<br /> <br /> Would it be in-theme for a Lunar to clone <i>just</i> one of his feet? A hank of his hair? A pint of blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-02-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:55:44-07:00","id":1099699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099693#post1099693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Just playing devil's advocate here\u2026)<br /> <br /> Would it be in-theme for a Lunar to clone <i>just</i> one of his feet? A hank of his hair? A pint of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, a Charm to grow multiple arms or additional legs isn't that much weirder than Charms to grow a pair of wings or more biological armor.<br /> <br /> Cloning more blood is sort of what Halting the Scarlet Flow does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T20:21:07-07:00","id":1099737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099699#post1099699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, a Charm to grow multiple arms or additional legs isn't that much weirder than Charms to grow a pair of wings or more biological armor.<br /> <br /> Cloning more blood is sort of what Halting the Scarlet Flow does.</div> </div> </div> </div>creating doubles feels a bit off. but its a common magic trick. but summon infinite copies is both easy to wank or seems limited for a lunar charm.<br /> <br /> eh duplicate things with that limit you mentioned though is akin to many pockets. you would need other practical limits. i know! scenelength commiment for items of value value equal to....your current willpower. versatile but prevented from cheesing.<br /> <br /> artifacts and so on count for double the value. if current rating drops below initial charm, and benefits, cease.<br /> <br /> this makes for a nice gss-alike with its own applicaptions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 06-02-2017, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T21:40:41-07:00","id":1099750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099699#post1099699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, a Charm to grow multiple arms or additional legs isn't that much weirder than Charms to grow a pair of wings or more biological armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say extra legs - I specified <i>just a foot</i>. It's not even attached to you, any more so than a cloned you would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T02:27:30-07:00","id":1099783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099687#post1099687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've already argued that Lunar Exalted can clone equipment together with clones; why does it suddenly become unthematic without a clone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is what I was worried about with the clones having equipment actually. I was aware that this might seem contradictory. It goes back a bit to what Isator was saying about how a Solar can make a daiklaive out of light but not, like, a chair, because one is mythically thematic and one isn't.<br /> <br /> See, I think the Lunar spawning extra copies of themselves* is fine. It's not something vitally thematic (I'd be quite happy for them to not have it, but I don't mind if it's something at the top of a tree that an Essence 4 or 5 Lunar could take), but it's thematic enough, I think.<br /> <br /> *BTW, I don't think a Lunar should gesture and have a copy of themselves appear out of nothing; I think they should grow the clone out of their skin, like an organism splitting into two.<br /> <br /> And, in fantasy literature and mythology, shapeshifters often absorb and later reproduce their clothes. And weapons I guess, are kind of like clothes (ie, when you turn into a dog, your sword vanishes, but it reappears again when you turn back into a human). So when they spawn extra copies of themselves, those come with clothes.<br /> <br /> But, just like a Lunar can transform themselves, including their clothes, but cannot ...<br /> <br /> Oh wait. Hmmm. I was going to say they can't change their clothes or weapons independently of their body, but actually they can, when wearing them. Or, could in 2nd ed anyway. So, spawning extra weapons... hmmm.<br /> <br /> Are Lunars still going to have the charm for changing their weapon into a different weapon? If they are, then I think a charm to split their weapon into two, in the same tree that allows them to split into two, would be okay.<br /> (But not 50 copies, because you can't hold 50 copies. When splitting, I think every copy should be touching the Lunar.)<br /> If that's not a charm they're still going to have, then they shouldn't be able to.<br /> (I still think it makes more sense as a Moonsilver Evocation than a Lunar charm. But it's not like splitting a sword into two swords is really powerful. It shouldn't be permanent though. No more than a scene, if it's a Lunar charm.)<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the problems with charms like this (cloning I mean) isn't the charm itself, but what it then leads people to argue should therefore be possible, that leads you off onto less thematic stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T05:45:01-07:00","id":1099795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099783#post1099783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is what I was worried about with the clones having equipment actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my own same worry from the very first post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was aware that this might seem contradictory. It goes back a bit to what Isator was saying about how a Solar can make a daiklaive out of light but not, like, a chair, because one is mythically thematic and one isn't. </div> </div> </div>As I said before in this thread, that's what <b>Words-As-Workshop Method </b>does. It can make damn near anything because it is a Craft Charm and not a Melee Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Words-as-Workshop Method</b><br /> the Exalt describes Artifact tools she needs to complete the present task, be it one of Craft, Lore, Medicine, Occult, or Investigation. The Essence of the world shapes itself into an artifact matching her description, with powers and active Evocations commensurate to the Exalt\u2019s description and the Storyteller\u2019s whims. The Exalt may use said Artifacts without paying an attunement cost, but if she wishes to lend them out, the borrower must pay an attunement cost in order to use them. Such Artifacts can be as simple or complex as needed, and may even have personalities. With each use of this Charm, the Solar may describe up to (Essence) tools, but the Storyteller should be aware of diminishing returns; the overall effectiveness should be based on the player\u2019s stunts and descriptions. In any case, these Artifact assistants allow for unspecified bonuses ranging from non-Charm dice, to the ability to listen for a daiklave\u2019s heartbeat, to holding a patient\u2019s soul in place while the Solar performs continual, complex surgery to fix horrific injury. Using Craftsman Needs No Tools with appropriate created Artifacts may allow the Exalt to work on superior or legendary Artifact projects at inopportune moments, with a stunt. Artifacts created by this Charm vanish in a blaze of Essence as soon as the Exalt is finished using them, or at the end of the scene, whichever comes first. </div> </div> </div>This Charm absolutely could let a Solar make an artifact table, for studying or crafting.<br /> <br /> It could let a Solar make an artifact bed, for treating someone who is injured or suffering from sleep deprivation.<br /> <br /> It can make a magical thinking chair that gives the Solar something comfortable to sit down and Sherlock Holmes upon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW, I don't think a Lunar should gesture and have a copy of themselves appear out of nothing; I think they should grow the clone out of their skin, like an organism splitting into two. </div> </div> </div>But Heart's Blood is magic, not DNA. The Liminal Exalted are the ones who care about biology and conservation of mass, since flesh and the acquisition of it are vital to their themes. Frankenstein's monster is rooted more solidly in science than the moon-tied wolfman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, in fantasy literature and mythology, shapeshifters often absorb and later reproduce their clothes. </div> </div> </div>Lunar Exalted traditionally banish such things to Elsewhere, rather than absorbed into their bodies. Because the Lunar Exalted are overtly magical rather than biological. Their theme is to be shamanic skinwalkers and face-stealing witches.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh wait. Hmmm. I was going to say they can't change their clothes or weapons independently of their body, but actually they can, when wearing them. Or, could in 2nd ed anyway. </div> </div> </div>Yes, a tiny little line in Changing Plummage mastery lets Lunars change their hair and clothes. I went looking for it earlier for the purposes of this thread, and I missed it the last time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Lunars still going to have the charm for changing their weapon into a different weapon? If they are, then I think a charm to split their weapon into two, in the same tree that allows them to split into two, would be okay. </div> </div> </div>At most, they could use Changing Plummage Mastery to change the <i>appearance </i>of the weapon, not the function. That Knack didn't let them turn clothes into functional armor.<br /> <br /> Besides, 3rd Edition is moving far away from the dramatic weapon-shifting of previous Editions of Lunar magic. In this edition, a daiklave that turns into a power-bow should be something special rather than trivial.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It shouldn't be permanent though. </div> </div> </div>I did say from the start that the cloned weapons would vanish shortly after leaving the Lunar's hand. As quickly as a Solar's Phantom Arrows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the problems with charms like this (cloning I mean) isn't the charm itself, but what it then leads people to argue should therefore be possible, that leads you off onto less thematic stuff. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for finally understanding my worries, which were the reason I created this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-03-2017, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T06:29:11-07:00","id":1099803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099750#post1099750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say extra legs - I specified <i>just a foot</i>. It's not even attached to you, any more so than a cloned you would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Solar use Glorious Solar Saber to make a sword without a blade, or a spearhead without a pole? <br /> <br /> Printed Charms are concerned with advantageous functions. Glorious Solar Saber and Twin Fang Technique naturally make a whole, functioning thing, rather than silly, useless things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T07:01:02-07:00","id":1099811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097782#post1097782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm not too sold on examining Faster Than Self to construct one's model for an equivalent Lunar Charm, especially since having it be unable to clone equipment will just lead to more &quot;Silver Solar&quot; mentality. Might be better to just blaze a new trail entirely, even if it gets to the same place.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097784#post1097784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I forgot to mention the advantage that the Lunar version would have: Compatibility with Stamina Charms.<br /> <br /> Faster Than Self Technique has to forbid interaction with any Resistance Charms that aren't permanent or Simple; the permanent Ox-Bodies are excluded since the Solar is set at Magnitude 10 regardless of Health Levels, and any Simple-type Resistance Charms need to be activated beforehand. Further, the Solar suffers a penalty to Athletics actions for three turns after Faster Than Self ends.<br /> <br /> The Lunar doesn't necessarily have that problem, since he's not actually running around pretending to multiple people at once. He actually is in multiple places at once, simultaneously. Much less exhausting.<br /> <br /> The Lunar might also be able to use the Stamina health-regeneration Charms to recover Magnitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alucard, I tried to answer your concerns about &quot;Silver Solar&quot; syndrome, but you haven't responded.<br /> <br /> Well, you did, but only to raise different questions or points.<br /> <br /> But do you have anything to say about these answers?<br /> <br /> How about these questions I asked you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097844#post1097844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why wouldn't <i>you </i>want to model mass Lunar cloning in a fashion similar to how Faster Than Self does it? What part do you disagree with?<br /> <br /> The large mote cost?<br /> <br /> The per-turn mote tax?<br /> <br /> Modeling the sheer number of bodies as a battle-group as opposed to a number of independent bodies? Giving a Lunar player the ability to act three or more times every round seems a tad much.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T07:46:29-07:00","id":1099822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097844#post1097844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part do you disagree with? The large mote cost? The per-turn mote tax? Modeling the sheer number of bodies as a battle-group as opposed to a number of independent bodies?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the above!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097844#post1097844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why wouldn't <i>you </i>want to model mass Lunar cloning in a fashion similar to how Faster Than Self does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because regardless of whether they're &quot;illusions under your control,&quot; or &quot;concentrated Lunar Essence forced into the form of your residual self-image,&quot; or &quot;a mass of you-tissue sprouted via your insane regeneration&quot; (or what-the-fuck-ever else Lunar Clone Technique ends up actually being), one thing they're <i>not</i> is &quot;you running fast enough to seem like a dozen men.&quot;<br /> <br /> Different things should <i>feel</i> different; giving them similar mechanics tends not to achieve that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1097844#post1097844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving a Lunar player the ability to act three or more times every round seems a tad much.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the love of Vance, could you give me a little more credit than that? I know one player going two or more times as often as the others is shitty; I said as much in other threads when discussing what I didn't like about the 2e tick-based system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T08:36:29-07:00","id":1099833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Well said,&quot; exclaimed Sun Wukong, &quot;spoken like a man. Come on then.&quot; The demon king dropped his guard to throw a punch, and Sun Wukong rushed in towards him, punching and kicking. When he spread out his hand it was enormous, and when he clenched his fist it was very hard. Sun Wukong hit the demon king in the ribs, kicked his backside, and smashed several of his joints. The demon king seized his steel sword that was as big as a plank, and swung it at Sun Wukong's skull. Sun Wukong dodged the blow, and the sword only split air.<br /> <br /> Seeing how ugly the demon king had turned, Sun Wukong used his magic art of getting extra bodies. He pulled out one of his hairs, popped it in his mouth, chewed it up, and blew it out into the air, shouting, &quot;Change!&quot; It turned into two or three hundred little monkeys, who all crowded round him.<br /> <br /> Sun Wukong now had an immortal body, and there was no magic transformation of which he was not capable. Since he had followed the Way he could change each of the eighty\u2212four thousand hairs on his body into anything he wanted. The little monkeys were too quick and nimble for sword or spear. </div> </div> </div>Took me a minute to find the text again, but here's Sun Wukong's method, which is one of the few things that comes to mind for self-replication in a mythic setting. I'm having trouble thinking of other examples off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T08:57:19-07:00","id":1099837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099822#post1099822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the above!</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not representing your ideas in a way that seems consistent.<br /> <br /> You say that you have no problem with Lunar Exalted using self-cloning to gain the advantages of a battle-group.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because regardless of whether they're &quot;illusions under your control,&quot; or &quot;concentrated Lunar Essence forced into the form of your residual self-image,&quot; or &quot;a mass of you-tissue sprouted via your insane regeneration&quot; (or what-the-fuck-ever else Lunar Clone Technique ends up actually being), one thing they're <i>not</i> is &quot;you running fast enough to seem like a dozen men.&quot;<br /> <br /> Different things should <i>feel</i> different; giving them similar mechanics tends not to achieve that.<br /> <br /> For the love of Vance, could you give me a little more credit than that? I know one player going two or more times as often as the others is shitty; I said as much in other threads when discussing what I didn't like about the 2e tick-based system. </div> </div> </div>You also argue that the Lunar Exalted should approach self-cloning in a way that is different from Faster-Than-Self Technique, whose principle effect is to give the Solar Exalt the advantages of a battle-group, with all other details being mere balancing pieces that would need to change to fit other Exalted attempting to use a similar effect.<br /> <br /> I do not understand your position at all.<br /> <br /> I have explained that I would want to see the Lunar version have different weaknesses and strengths compared to the Solar Charm, without one being strictly weaker than the other.<br /> <br /> Giving the Lunar version completely different kinds of prerequistes -- a combination of evasion and multi-attack Charms, I said -- was how I proposed to make the approach of the Lunar Charm feel different.<br /> <br /> I've also said that I'd like to see the Lunar Charm be available at lower Essence than Faster-Than-Self Technique, but that Lunar Exalted would have to start with battle-groups of Size 1 and find a way to work their way up to Faster Than Self's default of Size 3.<br /> <br /> Assuming for the sake of argument that you agree that Lunar Exalted could or should be able to use self-cloning to enjoy the advantages of being a battle-group, what more would you want in order to make the Lunar Charm feel different from the Solar Charm?<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming that you disagree, are you aware of the Backer-funded Solar Charm in <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted</i> that models a fighting collection of animals as a battle-group?<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099750#post1099750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say extra legs - I specified <i>just a foot</i>. It's not even attached to you, any more so than a cloned you would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Solar use Glorious Solar Saber to make a sword without a blade, or a spearhead without a pole?<br /> <br /> Printed Charms are concerned with advantageous functions. Glorious Solar Saber and Twin Fang Technique naturally make a whole, functioning thing, rather than silly, useless things.<br /> <br /> Vance said that a Charm which allowed Lunars to assume tiny versions of giant animals was possible and definitely thematic, but that it would be so useless and lame that it would never see print. It would be a parlor trick worthy only of stunting as a joke, not something to spend XP on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-03-2017, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T09:50:20-07:00","id":1099844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099795#post1099795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was my own same worry from the very first post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I didn't say anything until near the end of the 2nd page. You raised fair points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said before in this thread, that's what <b>Words-As-Workshop Method </b>does. It can make damn near anything because it is a Craft Charm and not a Melee Charm. </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that charm, admittedly (possibly because I dislike it, unlike summoning a golden sword of light out of your soul, which I think is rad).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Heart's Blood is magic, not DNA. The Liminal Exalted are the ones who care about biology and conservation of mass, since flesh and the acquisition of it are vital to their themes. Frankenstein's monster is rooted more solidly in science than the moon-tied wolfman. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't that that's really the issue, it's that their magic is about changing them, not changing things they are looking at. Like in the example Zale posted about Sun Wukong: he doesn't gesture and make monkeys appear, he turns his hair into monkeys.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunar Exalted traditionally banish such things to Elsewhere, rather than absorbed into their bodies. Because the Lunar Exalted are overtly magical rather than biological. Their theme is to be shamanic skinwalkers and face-stealing witches. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that really makes any differences. It's the same theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, a tiny little line in Changing Plummage mastery lets Lunars change their hair and clothes. I went looking for it earlier for the purposes of this thread, and I missed it the last time. </div> </div> </div>I do wonder if the writer thought that one through. I've used it a lot for all kinds of things. Being able to change your clothes, which seems to be the secondary use of that charm, seems far more useful than the primary use of changing your animal form a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At most, they could use Changing Plummage Mastery to change the <i>appearance </i>of the weapon, not the function. That Knack didn't let them turn clothes into functional armor. </div> </div> </div>I meant the one in Dex, clay-wetting practice or something, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, 3rd Edition is moving far away from the dramatic weapon-shifting of previous Editions of Lunar magic. In this edition, a daiklave that turns into a power-bow should be something special rather than trivial. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I half-remembered that. This is why I'm not sure about the cloning of weapons as a Lunar charm, but it seems fine as a conceivable moonsilver evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you for finally understanding my worries, which were the reason I created this thread. </div> </div> </div>It's nice to have a thread where we discuss the consequences of hypothetical charms and think them through, rather than just shout angrily about whether charm X ruins the game or not.<br /> (Well, in theory at least)<br /> <br /> After discussing it, have you decided on a conclusion?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T09:51:26-07:00","id":1099846,"title":"","content":"If a player came up with an instantaneous clone Charm - I don't know, &quot;Counterattack of the Clone&quot; in which the player instantly sprouts a clone in full equipment and uses it to launch a counterattack against anyone targeting him, I would allow the Lunar to perfectly duplicate the artifact weapon he is wielding. The Charm works quickly enough I would say that the Lunar manages to concentrate his Essence in such a way for such momentary period of time, he can copy his artifact equipment for that one attack and it's basically a glorified counterattack Charm.<br /> <br /> But if the player then came over and said, &quot;Hey, you know how when my character uses Counterattack of the Clone it creates a duplicate that includes my equipment? Well I came up with a new Charm I'm calling Artifact Duplicating Technique that just lets me make a perfect duplicate of any artifact my character is holding,&quot; I would tell the player no. While a Lunar might be able to perfectly duplicate his equipment for a single instant, he can't do so for any length of time.<br /> <br /> So if the Lunar had a, &quot;I make a bunch of clones of myself for mass combat&quot; type of Charm, those clones would look like the Lunar, and their equipment might look like the Lunar's, but <i>only</i> look like the Lunar's. Weapons and armor might be appear to be artifact weapons and armor but it would simply use mundane traits and not actually be treated as artifacts.<br /> <br /> This would be one of the differences between Faster Than Self (in which the Solar is just moving really, really, faster so each 'duplicate' is still always the same Solar). Of course, such a theoretical Lunar clone Charm would probably have other benefits as well and the potential to create clones would move well past simply being able to form a battlegroup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T10:02:33-07:00","id":1099849,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Lunars being able to turn into a horde of clones to fight (ie a battle group), would detract from their (very important and thematic) ability to turn into a swarm of tiny-to-small(-to-perhaps-medium) animals to fight (ie a battle group). Which, certainly, is going to be quite mechanically distinct from Faster than Self.<br /> <br /> And thus, it'd be better to keep Lunar cloning about spawning 1 or 2 useful servants (Ant and Starfish Trick? Was that the one in 2nd ed? But, you know, done better), rather than spawning 30 copies in the middle of combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T10:42:22-07:00","id":1099858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099844#post1099844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if the writer thought that one through. I've used it a lot for all kinds of things. Being able to change your clothes, which seems to be the secondary use of that charm, seems far more useful than the primary use of changing your animal form a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I'm not sure about the cloning of weapons as a Lunar charm, but it seems fine as a conceivable moonsilver evocation. </div> </div> </div>Well, I think I'll address this when answering the next person.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's nice to have a thread where we discuss the consequences of hypothetical charms and think them through, rather than just shout angrily about whether charm X ruins the game or not.<br /> (Well, in theory at least) </div> </div> </div>Thank you, and you're welcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After discussing it, have you decided on a conclusion? </div> </div> </div>Not yet.<br /> <br /> See, I think my approach to debate is to take the side I most strongly agree with already, and then advocate that position as strongly and honestly as I can. I then hope for someone else to do the same thing with an opposing position; my devil's advocate.<br /> <br /> The goal is to test the validity of both positions against each other. We both attempt to respectfully explain our positions as best as we can, and to sound out any weaknesses in the other's position. We do not ignore any good points the opponent makes, or move the goal posts, because the purpose isn't winning an argument, but rather to examine both sides of the issue.<br /> <br /> I examine someone else's points, and if I come to agree with their position more than my own, I change position. Since I have examined both sides of the debate, I feel confident that I have a proper understanding of the situation and the best answer to the problem.<br /> <br /> If someone examines my points and comes to agree with my position, then I feel confident that my position is valid.<br /> <br /> <br /> As yet, no one seems convinced, and I don't think we're done exploring the issue from both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 09-17-2017, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:00:16-07:00","id":1099859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099846#post1099846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player came up with an instantaneous clone Charm - I don't know, &quot;Counterattack of the Clone&quot; in which the player instantly sprouts a clone in full equipment and uses it to launch a counterattack against anyone targeting him, I would allow the Lunar to perfectly duplicate the artifact weapon he is wielding. The Charm works quickly enough I would say that the Lunar manages to concentrate his Essence in such a way for such momentary period of time, he can copy his artifact equipment for that one attack and it's basically a glorified counterattack Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the clone doesn't need a cloned weapon in that case. The clone could emerge from the Lunar in such a way that it comes away holding the Lunar's weapon, and after it attacks the enemy, it tosses the weapon back to the Lunar as it disappears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if the player then came over and said, &quot;Hey, you know how when my character uses Counterattack of the Clone it creates a duplicate that includes my equipment? Well I came up with a new Charm I'm calling Artifact Duplicating Technique that just lets me make a perfect duplicate of any artifact my character is holding,&quot; I would tell the player no. While a Lunar might be able to perfectly duplicate his equipment for a single instant, he can't do so for any length of time. </div> </div> </div>Okay, that is your position, and I respect your position, but I want to examine why you hold that position.<br /> <br /> Dual-wielding twin weapons isn't actually advantageous in 3rd Edition the same way it was before. The only mechanical benefit is getting a +2 clash bonus and still having a weapon after someone succeeds at a disarming gambit against you. Anything more than that requires dual-wielding two completely different kinds of weapons, or else using Charms like Steel Devil Style.<br /> <br /> Even if a Lunar duplicated Volcano Cutter, he's not really doing himself any favors. He can still only attack once with it per turn, and it doesn't have any Evocations where dual-wielding would increase its damage or scope of effect. The copy of Volcano Cutter would even need to build up its own store of motes in order to activate its first Evocation, which means the Lunar would need to make twice as many attacks to charge it up.<br /> <br /> Further, the copy would vanish as soon as the Lunar lets go of it. It might last long enough to hit someone if he threw it at them, but not long enough for anyone else to use it for themselves. So the Lunar cannot just hand copies of Volcano Cutter out to the rest of his party-members.<br /> <br /> Those are the reasons why I think Twin Fang Technique would not be broken. Do you have any other concerns?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if the Lunar had a, &quot;I make a bunch of clones of myself for mass combat&quot; type of Charm, those clones would look like the Lunar, and their equipment might look like the Lunar's, but <i>only</i> look like the Lunar's. Weapons and armor might be appear to be artifact weapons and armor but it would simply use mundane traits and not actually be treated as artifacts. </div> </div> </div>That would not really bother me, even though I'm not sure it is necessary.<br /> <br /> There could be potential brokenness if the Lunar battle-group with their dozen copies of Volcano Cutter are able to make one non-magical area-of-effect attack against everyone in their range band, as battle-groups can do. A player might argue that each copy of Volcano Cutter was able to make a separate attack and thus he charged up all 12 for using the weapon's first Evocation.<br /> <br /> I would deny him in this case on account of balance. It was enough that all enemies treated the attack as having the traits of a grand daiklave, but effectively only one Volcano Cutter received the charge, so only one could unleash the fire-blast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, such a theoretical Lunar clone Charm would probably have other benefits as well and the potential to create clones would move well past simply being able to form a battlegroup. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it has already come up that a Lunar might be able to create one (or a small number) of weaker, longer-lived clones, and I also hope that temporary clones for distracting evasions and attacks will come before or after the battle-group Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:05:35-07:00","id":1099860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099849#post1099849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Lunars being able to turn into a horde of clones to fight (ie a battle group), would detract from their (very important and thematic) ability to turn into a swarm of tiny-to-small(-to-perhaps-medium) animals to fight (ie a battle group). Which, certainly, is going to be quite mechanically distinct from Faster than Self.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them as two completely different tricks, thematically and mechanically.<br /> <br /> A Lunar who clones himself occupies more space and multiplies his effective power.<br /> <br /> A Lunar who turns into a swarm instead divides himself; he doesn't multiply his power, but rather trades one form of power for a completely different form of power. He loses the ability to make feats of strength (except to chew through things), he cannot use any of his weapons, and he cannot parry attacks, but he becomes better able to evade attacks and perform distraction gambits for his allies.<br /> <br /> This is why I think the power to become a swarm grows from the power to become a small creature, whereas I think the power to multiple oneself is not inherently tied to becoming small or large.<br /> <br /> But even if they are different, they are not incompatible; a Lunar can combine the power to subdivide with the power to multiply. Instead of becoming a swarm only as big as a man in total, he can use both tricks together to instead become a swarm as large as an army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:14:54-07:00","id":1099861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099859#post1099859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any other concerns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two issues.<br /> <br /> First, allowing players to create perfect duplicates of held items is potentially very game breaking. While <i>at this moment</i> I can't think of anything that could cause problems, we also only have one real book in the gameline. As the gameline continues we'll be seeing more material getting published, and eventually I wouldn't be surprised if being able to duplicate any kind of held item could result in seeing some fairly game breaking shennanigans. I would just prefer to avoid that.<br /> <br /> Second, and more importantly, I just don't see making duplicates of held items as something that is really in the Lunar's thematic wheelhouse. This seems like it would be a decent Charm for Alchemicals - maybe they have a Charm that allows them to temporarily convert that Charm into a sub-set of different items that they're carrying. But ultimately, duplicating and copying tools just doesn't feel like a Lunar Charm to me.<br /> <br /> Copying yourself? Yeah, I can see that as a Lunar Charm.<br /> Copying yourself and your gear, at least visually though not mechanically? Yeah, alright - otherwise when you make your copies you'll have to deal with buttnekkid Lunars.<br /> Just copying your gear and letting it retain its full power and not copying anything else? Nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:27:13-07:00","id":1099865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099861#post1099861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, allowing players to create perfect duplicates of held items is potentially very game breaking. While <i>at this moment</i> I can't think of anything that could cause problems, we also only have one real book in the gameline. As the gameline continues we'll be seeing more material getting published, and eventually I wouldn't be surprised if being able to duplicate any kind of held item could result in seeing some fairly game breaking shennanigans. I would just prefer to avoid that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is a strong concern.<br /> <br /> Even though I was able to patch over potential brokenness in my own example, it was a patch that would have been hard or undesirable to codify in the Lunar battle-group Charm itself, and probably not the only possible example of a broken interaction.<br /> <br /> Far better to just deny any possibility of an artifact's Evocations getting cloned, and that includes attunement bonuses.<br /> <br /> However, I do not necessarily agree that this means the cloned weapons should be treated as mundane weapons in terms of basic traits like Accuracy and Damage. Especially on the battle-group scale, this means that the Lunar with his single artifact weapon finds its superior traits lost in the mass of mundane weapon traits used by his battle-group of clones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, and more importantly, I just don't see making duplicates of held items as something that is really in the Lunar's thematic wheelhouse. This seems like it would be a decent Charm for Alchemicals - maybe they have a Charm that allows them to temporarily convert that Charm into a sub-set of different items that they're carrying. But ultimately, duplicating and copying tools just doesn't feel like a Lunar Charm to me. </div> </div> </div>I think Alchemicals can approach self-cloning through &quot;quantum uncertainty&quot; manipulation engines, which would allow them to create temporary distraction clones for evasion and attack, counter-attack clones such as you suggested earlier, and even full-blown battle-group clones. And yes, also weapon-cloning.<br /> <br /> Though the weapon-cloning would be more of a neat submodule to cover useful edge cases, rather than a workhorse Charm by itself. Because unlike Lunar Exalted, the Alchemical Exalted actually can have Charms like Glorious Solar Saber and Immaculate Golden Bow. Transcendent Multi-modal Artifact Matrix, I think it was called.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what feels &quot;Lunar&quot;, it feels acceptable to me that if a Lunar can create cloned weapons for his cloned bodies, then he can clone weapons <i>without </i>cloned bodies, in order to have an endless supply of throwing implements for as long he holds the original and has the motes to spend.<br /> <br /> Saying that he can do the first and not the second feels very arbitrary and artificial, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:40:49-07:00","id":1099868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099865#post1099865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I do not necessarily agree that this means the cloned weapons should be treated as mundane weapons in terms of basic traits like Accuracy and Damage. Especially on the battle-group scale, this means that the Lunar with his single artifact weapon finds its superior traits lost in the mass of mundane weapon traits used by his battle-group of clones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an issue with this, especially if this theoretical Lunar battlegroup clone Charm came with other benefits to even if it out. This would help to make it mechanically distinct and different from Faster Than Self. But then like I said earlier in the thread, I don't even think Lunars should be able to make so many clones of their human-form, equipment wielding selves that they can create a battlegroup out of them in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099865#post1099865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what feels &quot;Lunar&quot;, it feels acceptable to me that if a Lunar can create cloned weapons for his cloned bodies, then he can clone weapons <i>without </i>cloned bodies, in order to have an endless supply of throwing implements for as long he holds the original and has the motes to spend.<br /> <br /> Saying that he can do the first and not the second feels very arbitrary and artificial, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think duplicating artifacts feels like something Lunars should be able to do as a general thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T12:06:35-07:00","id":1099879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099868#post1099868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have an issue with this, especially if this theoretical Lunar battlegroup clone Charm came with other benefits to even if it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This would help to make it mechanically distinct and different from Faster Than Self. </div> </div> </div>Would it? The artifact issue would be effectively the same as for Solars, who also use the basic artifact traits for the whole battle-group but who practically only have one artifact to use, Evocation-wise, and only as many arrows or throwing projectiles as the Solar started with or pays for with Charms.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger difference is letting the Lunar battle-group freely use Lunar Stamina Charms, without Faster-Than-Self's restriction against Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then like I said earlier in the thread, I don't even think Lunars should be able to make so many clones of their human-form, equipment wielding selves that they can create a battlegroup out of them in the first place. </div> </div> </div>A battle-group of Size 1 is roughly twelve dudes, and that feels big enough for a Lunar start. Faster-Than-Self Technique by default allows a Solar to become a Size 3 battle-group, which the book defines as &quot;over a hundred combatants&quot;.<br /> <br /> I feel like a Lunar getting up to a Size 3 battle-group should be a high-end accomplishment, whereas a Size 1 group is a middle or high-middle level achievement.<br /> <br /> Even if the Lunar Charm does end up being a Dexterity 5, Essence 5 Charm with seven or eight prerequisites, equal to Faster-Than-Self, I prefer the more intimate size of a Size 1 battle-group as a start. I'd rather start out at Naruto's lower end of Shadow Clone no Jutsu before working to achieve the Mass Shadow Clone no Jutsu.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just don't think duplicating artifacts feels like something Lunars should be able to do as a general thing. </div> </div> </div>But I hope you can provide a justification for why you think the divide isn't artificial or arbitrary.<br /> <br /> I'd like to share your position, but I will not ignore this obstacle. I want a solution to this problem that I can present to someone else who has the same problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T08:36:00-07:00","id":1100144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1098388#post1098388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBack to the cloning, I think their weapons would be evenly distributed regardless of an inability to conjure a new weapon individually, because I don't think the Charms of anybody should be constructed according to that logic. It's the same as how a Solar being able to evoke a magic weapon from their spirit doesn't equate to being able to shape objects in general from sunlight and soul stuff, because the magic doesn't have a reductive element; there isn't an element that you can break down and reorganize to do something different, it's a capability that arises from a singular purpose informed by a narrative and erroneous human perception and categorization.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099050#post1099050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLike I said, it's the same as how Glorious Solar Saber does not mean that Solars can conjure absolutely anything, because it's not about shaping hard light being applied to a function, it's about the mythic warrior being able to draw a weapon from within themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator, do you want to reconsider your stance after being reminded about Words-As-Workshop Method?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Apologies, I was mistaken about the exact point being argued here. Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-04-2017, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T08:48:56-07:00","id":1100147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100144#post1100144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator, do you want to reconsider your stance after being reminded about Words-As-Workshop Method?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would he? He was talking about Glorious Solar Saber, not Words-As-Workshop Method.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about how Charm A works like X, Charm B working like Y generally has no bearing on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T08:55:02-07:00","id":1100149,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, welcome back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099822#post1099822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the above!</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not representing your ideas in a way that seems consistent.<br /> <br /> You say that you have no problem with Lunar Exalted using self-cloning to gain the advantages of a battle-group.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because regardless of whether they're &quot;illusions under your control,&quot; or &quot;concentrated Lunar Essence forced into the form of your residual self-image,&quot; or &quot;a mass of you-tissue sprouted via your insane regeneration&quot; (or what-the-fuck-ever else Lunar Clone Technique ends up actually being), one thing they're <i>not</i> is &quot;you running fast enough to seem like a dozen men.&quot;<br /> <br /> Different things should <i>feel</i> different; giving them similar mechanics tends not to achieve that.<br /> <br /> For the love of Vance, could you give me a little more credit than that? I know one player going two or more times as often as the others is shitty; I said as much in other threads when discussing what I didn't like about the 2e tick-based system. </div> </div> </div>You also argue that the Lunar Exalted should approach self-cloning in a way that is different from Faster-Than-Self Technique, whose principle effect is to give the Solar Exalt the advantages of a battle-group, with all other details being mere balancing pieces that would need to change to fit other Exalted attempting to use a similar effect.<br /> <br /> I do not understand your position at all.<br /> <br /> I have explained that I would want to see the Lunar version have different weaknesses and strengths compared to the Solar Charm, without one being strictly weaker than the other.<br /> <br /> Giving the Lunar version completely different kinds of prerequistes -- a combination of evasion and multi-attack Charms, I said -- was how I proposed to make the approach of the Lunar Charm feel different.<br /> <br /> I've also said that I'd like to see the Lunar Charm be available at lower Essence than Faster-Than-Self Technique, but that Lunar Exalted would have to start with battle-groups of Size 1 and find a way to work their way up to Faster Than Self's default of Size 3.<br /> <br /> Assuming for the sake of argument that you agree that Lunar Exalted could or should be able to use self-cloning to enjoy the advantages of being a battle-group, what more would you want in order to make the Lunar Charm feel different from the Solar Charm?<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming that you disagree, are you aware of the Backer-funded Solar Charm in <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted</i> that models a fighting collection of animals as a battle-group?<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1099750#post1099750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say extra legs - I specified <i>just a foot</i>. It's not even attached to you, any more so than a cloned you would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Solar use Glorious Solar Saber to make a sword without a blade, or a spearhead without a pole?<br /> <br /> Printed Charms are concerned with advantageous functions. Glorious Solar Saber and Twin Fang Technique naturally make a whole, functioning thing, rather than silly, useless things.<br /> <br /> Vance said that a Charm which allowed Lunars to assume tiny versions of giant animals was possible and definitely thematic, but that it would be so useless and lame that it would never see print. It would be a parlor trick worthy only of stunting as a joke, not something to spend XP on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T09:05:28-07:00","id":1100151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, welcome back.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I didn't reply to something earlier, please don't try and pressure me to reply to it now. <i>I saw it</i>, and while slapping me in the face with it might provoke me to answer, I won't appreciate it.<br /> <br /> (I'd also rather you not do it to others, but I can't speak for them.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not representing your ideas in a way that seems consistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please forgive me for not having a master Alucard document where all my ideas are extensively collated by a team of researchers, so that I can make a point one day and seamlessly pick back up on that same point days later. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that you have no problem with Lunar Exalted using self-cloning to gain the advantages of a battle-group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also argue that the Lunar Exalted should approach self-cloning in a way that is different from Faster-Than-Self Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026whose principle effect is to give the Solar Exalt the advantages of a battle-group, <b>with all other details being mere balancing pieces that would need to change to fit other Exalted attempting to use a similar effect.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that the selected clause in this bit is necessarily true. A lot of it seems keyed to the idea that the Solar is moving fast, as opposed to conjuring phantom warriors out of fire or growing them out of his body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand your position at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I've got it hammered out all that solidly, I must admit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming for the sake of argument that you agree that Lunar Exalted could or should be able to use self-cloning to enjoy the advantages of being a battle-group, what more would you want in order to make the Lunar Charm feel different from the Solar Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that you disagree, are you aware of the Backer-funded Solar Charm in <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted</i> that models a fighting collection of animals as a battle-group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming I disagree, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100149#post1100149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar use Glorious Solar Saber to make a sword without a blade, or a spearhead without a pole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious Solar Saber doesn't make spears, but even if it did, you're missing the point - Glorious Solar Saber makes a whole sword, and doesn't upgrade to let you make just a handle. If the hypothetical Lunar clone Charm makes a whole you, it presumably follows that <i>it also</i> wouldn't let you make just a piece of you (because, to a Charm that clones you, that's what your sword <i>is</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-04-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T09:18:36-07:00","id":1100157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1100151#post1100151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I didn't reply to something earlier, please don't try and pressure me to reply to it now. <i>I saw it</i>, and while slapping me in the face with it might provoke me to answer, I won't appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I supposed to appreciate you raising arguments that don't hold up under basic scrutiny and then getting nothing but silence when I ask you for explanation?<br /> <br /> I value your input because you're a smart dude with opinions I can agree with, but sometimes it feels like you're just being negative for the sake of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:54:51-07:00","id":1140982,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140402#post1140402\">In another thread recently</a>, you argued that, like the Sidereal Exalted, the Lunar Exalted could do weird things like take intangible conditions of the world and physically manifest those things as creatures.<br /> <br /> Does that mean you've changed your mind about a Lunar Exalt being able to make an exact physical copy of a weapon he's holding, such that he could hold a spear in one hand and throw an endless supply of cloned spears from his other, with the cloned spears disappearing after they strike like the missiles of Solar Phantom Arrow Technique?<br /> <br /> <br /> With Lunar Exalted aesthetics opening up from &quot;internal strength&quot; to &quot;warrior, trickster, shaman&quot;, I think that if Lunar Exalted can do weird witch-doctor things like turn diseases into creatures, they can do witch-warrior things like turning their Essence into copies of a weapon they already hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's pretty sneaky to go back and edit your late answers into a previous post. Did you actually want me to know those were there? You should know that the system won't alert me to such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 09-17-2017, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:11:56-07:00","id":1141180,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on Lunar Cloning:<br /> <br /> 1. Lunar battle group forming charms ought to be &quot;I turn into a swarm of bats,&quot; or &quot;I turn into a pack of wolves,&quot; or &quot;I turn my hairs into a small army of angry monkeys.&quot; They shouldn't be &quot;I make twelve more of me.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. To the extent that Lunars are able to clone themselves, we shouldn't be looking to the Solar &quot;The Flash&quot; charms for inspiration. We should be looking to the Mirror Flag charms! A Solar can create a multitude of strangers within herself; a Lunar ought to be able to divide herself into multiple people with different capabilities. Rather than inventing fake personalities from whole cloth, though, a Lunar should be using what she's already got-one clone might have her intimacy of love for her children and her Stamina charms, one clone might have her hatred for the Realm and know her Martial Arts style, etc. The difference between this and Yozi soul-heirarchy stuff would be that the Lunar loses the things she gives to her Clones, and gets them back when the clones are destroyed. I like the idea of a powerful lunar having trouble making a decision splitting into multiple people to argue about it. I like the idea of a Lunar clone who only has one or two charms and just one extra animal shape to change into as a low level antagonist for a mortal or DB party who can foreshadow the greater enemy of which he is part. I like the idea that a PC who is going to have to miss game for a session or two could say, &quot;I'll split off a clone and give her three of my Medicine dots and my healing-your-allies charms to back you guys up without you needing to worry about my combat charms, and the rest of me will go do an offscreen sidequest while I'm gone.&quot; Committing parts of yourself to different character sheets ought to be a bit dangerous-I'd make PCs divide their Health Levels up between the clones as well, and the ones without the Stamina charms don't get the benefits of those charms, and a clone getting killed should give you those levels back but full of damage.<br /> <br /> 3. I like the idea of clones left on their own too long developing their own intimacies and being reluctant to return to the main Lunar when their mission is done, and I like the idea of the main Lunar's player gaining the option of absorbing those memories and intimacies when they reabsorb the clone (because that generates more plot potential than just devouring them). I also like the idea of clones who don't know they're clones, so you can have someone turn in terror to someone they thought was their friend and be like, &quot;Wait...Chen hates spicy foods. You're the Anathema, aren't you?!&quot; and have the Lunar smile and say, &quot;No, Shin. YOU are the Anathema.&quot; Lunar sleeper agents could be fun and add interesting dynamics to their cold war with the Sidereals. Sidereals having to murder relative innocents for the greater good is always a good idea, and Lunar games involving questions about what identity means in the absence of a fixed shape are also good ideas.<br /> <br /> 4. I like the idea that you have a limited number of shapes to share between your clones. You don't make three identical copies of yourself, you have one that looks like you and one that looks like that guy you ate yesterday and one that looks like his dog which you also ate yesterday. Playing &quot;which is the real me,&quot; is like playing &quot;which cup is the bean under-&quot; it's a con, and the real you is the fourth shape that's an ant slowly crawling away hoping not to get noticed in the kung-fu fray. Why disguise yourself as yourself when you have so many better disguises immediately available?<br /> <br /> 4. Lunars shouldn't be able to create duplicate items. If your combat style is based on your cool artifact axe, the cloning tree shouldn't give you five guys and five cool artifact axes. I'm cool with clones not arriving naked, because while hilarious the first time that gets old quick, so I'm alright with the cloning charm equipping the clone at creation with suitable clothing and any items you have stored in Elsewhere that you wanna share. Maybe you give the Clone your two dots in performance and that artifact Lute you have sitting in Elsewhere and your Manipulation and Appearance charms: keep your cool artifact axe for yourself and send him off to seduce the local princess.<br /> <br /> 5. Killing the original should kill all the Lunar's clones. Wyld Hunts should remain possible and credible threats against Lunar PCs who have the Clone Myself Tree, which means that Wyld Hunt becomes a traditional &quot;hunt down Dracula because if we kill him it kills all his offspring,&quot; plot. Bonus points if a clone has turned against the Lunar and is your friend and you know that killing the Lunar will kill your new friend.<br /> <br /> 6. THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT ONE: You know the whole, &quot;extra actions are unfair,&quot; thing? The solution to that is that Lunar clones are NPCs. They're not bound to your will like a demon. You create them, and they have the intimacies and knowledge you give them at their creation, so they're usually on your side...but the longer they're separated from you the more they become their own people. You're weaker while they exist, and while they have a vested interest in your continued survival so they probably won't try to kill you...they also have a tendency to not want to get reabsorbed after they start building their own lives. Clones should be costly to create compared to swarm/animal battle group charms to discourage pumping out a ton of them in combat, and using the charm should be understood by all as trading some of your own power for some dots in Ally. I don't want people to never take these charms, so I'd say the Clone requires a committed mote cost and dies when you decommit the motes, returning your charms/HLs to you...but if only you actually physically reabsorb the clone in person do you also get their memories/intimacies. I'd be open to reabsorbing clones who have gone off and learned new things being a way to make an XP engine or get around training times kinda like Solar Teaching charms, which gives busy Lunars a reason to give up some of their power for long term clones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-17-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:24:34-07:00","id":1141207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1141180#post1141180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts on Lunar Cloning:<br /> <br /> 1. Lunar battle group forming charms ought to be &quot;I turn into a swarm of bats,&quot; or &quot;I turn into a pack of wolves,&quot; or &quot;I turn my hairs into a small army of angry monkeys.&quot; They shouldn't be &quot;I make twelve more of me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Wukong totally made twelve more of himself.<br /> <br /> He made an ARMY of himself, which is the source of inspiration I'm driving at.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. To the extent that Lunars are able to clone themselves, we shouldn't be looking to the Solar &quot;The Flash&quot; charms for inspiration. We should be looking to the Mirror Flag charms! A Solar can create a multitude of strangers within herself; a Lunar ought to be able to divide herself into multiple people with different capabilities. </div> </div> </div>But we're not talking about Personae effects.<br /> <br /> Yes, Lunar cloning should probably interact with Lunar alternate Personae capabilities, but Personae effects are not my focus in this thread.<br /> <br /> But if you want to make a thread to explore those ideas for Lunar alternate Personae, I'm all for it. I tried homebrewing various Charms for such a path, including giving Personae their own Totems and possibly even different Castes!<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, long-term duration clones are a bit beyond the scope I intended for discussion. I wanted to talk about scene-long and instant-duration effects.<br /> <br /> I think your Personae ideas are a good way to look into placing limitations upon clones which last far longer than that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Lunars shouldn't be able to create duplicate items. If your combat style is based on your cool artifact axe, the cloning tree shouldn't give you five guys and five cool artifact axes. </div> </div> </div>So you disagree with Robert Vance that Lunar Exalted can or should have a Charm to become a battle-group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T15:25:41-07:00","id":1141228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1141207#post1141207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you disagree with Robert Vance that Lunar Exalted can or should have a Charm to become a battle-group?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with them becoming a battle group (though I would prefer swarmform for that)! But if we let you make a dozen short term copies of yourself (which, Sun Wukong or no, I am not about, I don't like the feel), only one of 'em oughta have your fancy magic axe.<br /> <br /> This axe thing cuts to the heart of why I prefer personae style clone charms or none at all. Anytime you duplicate yourself in a game that includes a semblance of balance, you run into the need for the duplicates to be weaker than you to balance them, with a sort of inverse ninja principle. A battle group of you isn't fifty full powered Lunar warriors, it's you plus a bunch of watered down mini-yous. If you're wearing the Crown of Thunders, you don't get to make a bunch of mini Crowns of Thunders, it cheapens the feel of an irreproducable legendary wonder to make a bunch of cheap knockoffs. And that's before the &quot;I make fifty copies of the Soulbreaker Orb and fly in a directions&quot; shenanigans. There's something off about the very feeling of duplicating gear that I think is the reason we're having a discussion about it. That feeling goes away for me when the duplicates are using claws and teeth.<br /> <br /> I feel that if you want a Battle Group of You, the original you with your magic axe oughta be acting as a Commander for that Battle Group-Lunars don't usually get telepathy, after all, instant wordless communication between human forms requires charms for a reason...but I expect you'll find that idea unsatisfying because it plays out as a &quot;make a battle group to command&quot; charm instead of a &quot;turn into a battle group&quot; charm. It's cool to have a swarm of bats or a cloud of wasps or maybe even at the far end a pack of wolves or clawstriders acting with a single purpose because that fits into the Lunar combination of monster and nature tropes. With human forms, though? Nah, I am not into it.<br /> <br /> I would much rather keep the number of clones small and require investment in each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T16:32:14-07:00","id":1141248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1141228#post1141228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with them becoming a battle group (though I would prefer swarmform for that)! But if we let you make a dozen short term copies of yourself (which, Sun Wukong or no, I am not about, I don't like the feel), only one of 'em oughta have your fancy magic axe.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only one member of a battlegroup has an axe, then the axe fails to factor into the battlegroup's attacks.<br /> <br /> Specifically attacking with the axe would be a normal, single-target attack made without any of the benefits of a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're wearing the Crown of Thunders, you don't get to make a bunch of mini Crowns of Thunders, it cheapens the feel of an irreproducable legendary wonder to make a bunch of cheap knockoffs. </div> </div> </div>They're temporary and vanish from existence. Plus, they might not even have the magical abilities of the original, just the physical properties.<br /> <br /> ALSO, you presume that there's &quot;an original&quot; in the group. As opposed to the Lunar evenly subdividing his body, mind, and Essence into multiple bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that if you want a Battle Group of You, the original you with your magic axe oughta be acting as a Commander for that Battle Group. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea, which could certainly be used to impose limits on your clones that would not apply to you, and would also further distinguish the Charm from Faster-Than-Self Technique.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this denies you the protections afforded by being an entire crowd.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a related note, I'm trying to decide how satisfying it would be to have your battlegroup of identical clones punch someone first, and then you punch next to take advantage of the onslaught penalty.<br /> <br /> It seems less immediately satisfying than BEING a battlegroup of yourself and punching someone, but there is a definite narrative parallel to Naruto's &quot;Naruto Rendan&quot; attack, where he uses his clones to execute a combination of attacks that leaves a target open (ie: facing an onslaught penalty) to Naruto's own attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars don't usually get telepathy, after all </div> </div> </div>The issue is neatly avoided if the Lunar is DIVIDING himself into battlegroup, rather than creating additional bodies as external fakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}